= Scientific literature =

== Overview ==
The '''scientific literature''' is the body of recorded scientific works through which research questions, methods, evidence, analyses, results, interpretations, and critiques are communicated.

It includes journal articles, conference papers, books, reports, preprints, data papers, and other research outputs depending on field and purpose.

The scientific literature is a communication record, not the totality of scientific knowledge. Individual works can be incomplete, disputed, superseded, corrected, or retracted.

== Boundaries ==
* scientific literature ≠ all scientific knowledge
* publication ≠ correctness
* one paper ≠ scientific consensus

